Spec: Isolated Android FRP bridge coordinator

Purpose:
  Combine native Keystore identity and actual Android transport with the existing Windows publisher and authenticated Go backend.

Owns:
  ./AndroidFixture.cs

Must:
  Require the explicitly isolated headless x86_64 emulator and ADB port5038 for every device command; never discover or operate a physical phone.
  Specify the existing remote loopback ADB host so a lost isolated server cannot cause the client to launch a replacement discovery server.
  Transfer only public enrollment material and target-private fixture inputs, never command-line secrets or private device keys.
  Hold owned instrumentation processes, bound waits and record actual relay bytes separately from SDK/native-UID and physical NAT acceptance.

  Exercise the owner-started server-configured gateway from an independently signed SDK-only application; verify real bytes, concurrent private runtime instances and separate local/server revocation before reporting public Android SDK acceptance.

  Verify actual runtime reuse and that cancelling a shared stream leaves the other business stream alive.

  Supply the actual authenticated publisher IPv4 port for direct SDK verification and record the selected LAN or XTCP candidate separately from physical NAT acceptance.
  Assert one pooled runtime before exercising a different authorized scope; different scopes must not share a runtime merely to satisfy an aggregate count.
  Exercise formal public open/status/attach/close through the independent SDK, verify exact actual counters and invalidate a test-owned network generation without changing real device networking.
  Hold a silent owned loopback TCP listener for the alternate approved route and refresh local grants before requiring cold XTCP; never substitute an external address or wrong identity for a transport failure.
